                                      :RegularizationOnValueFairness ,
                                      :ReplaceStereotypes ,
                                      :UserItemReRanking ;
        resource:SIO_000068 :EU_AI_Act ;
        rdfs:comment "Sets obligations for distributors of high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance at market placement (e.g., presence of required documentation/instructions and integrity of the supplied system), cooperate with competent authorities, and take actions when non-compliance or risks are suspected. Notes: Distributor-side role is assurance: verify the provider’s conformity package (incl. fairness indicators/limits and declared controls) is present and not neutralised by integration/packaging choices; if issues arise, coordinate corrective actions and preserve traceability to the supplied version." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.25
:Art.25 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                 :LegalRequirement ,
                 :ManagementLegalRequirement ;
        :isOperationalizedBy :Calibration ,
                             :CounterfactualFairness ,
                             :DemographicParity ,
                             :EqualOpportunity ,
                             :EqualizedOdds ,
                             :MatchingConditionalFrequencies ,
                             :StatisticalParity ,
                             :TestFairness ;
        resource:SIO_000068 :EU_AI_Act ;
        rdfs:comment "Clarifies responsibilities along the AI value chain for high-risk AI systems, including when another actor becomes the provider (e.g., branding, substantial modification, or purpose change) and related cooperation duties between actors. Notes: Value-chain governance: notions/metrics are mapped as handover anchors for fairness evidence. If accountability shifts, the new provider must inherit and/or regenerate the mapped evidence and monitoring, traceable to the modified version and context of use." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/Art.26
:Art.26 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                 :LegalRequirement ,
                 :ManagementLegalRequirement ;
        :isOperationalizedBy :Calibration ,
