###  http://fairness_ontology.com/ChangeAttentionScores
:ChangeAttentionScores rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                :HeadOnly ,
                                :MitigationTechnique ,
                                :ModelAccessResourcesMitigation ,
                                :PartialFineTuning ,
                                :ScientificArtifact ,
                                :TrainingResourcesMitigation ,
                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                  owl:onProperty :isAppliedAt ;
                                  owl:allValuesFrom :In-processing
                                ] ;
                       :isProposedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2022_GACI> ;
                       :isUsedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2022_GACI> ;
                       :supportsComplianceWith :Art.15 ,
                                               :Art.53 ;
                       :scientificArtifactDescription "Address stereotypes learned in the attention layer of sentence-level encoders by redistributing attention scores, fine-tuning the encoder with an equalization loss that encourages equal attention scores (e.g., to attend to “doctor”) with respect to each social group (e.g., “he” and “she”), while minimizing changes to the attention of other words in the sentence. The equalization loss is added as a regularization term to a semantic information preservation term that computes the distance between the original and fine-tuned models’ attention scores." .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/ChangeAttentionWeights
:ChangeAttentionWeights rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                 :MitigationTechnique ,
                                 :ModelAccessResourcesMitigation ,
                                 :PartialFineTuning ,
                                 :ScientificArtifact ,
                                 :SelectiveParameterUpdating ,
                                 :TrainingResourcesMitigation ,
                                 [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                   owl:onProperty :isAppliedAt ;
                                   owl:allValuesFrom :In-processing
                                 ] ;
                        :isProposedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2023_ZAYED> ;
                        :isUsedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2023_ZAYED> ;
                        :supportsComplianceWith :Art.15 ,
                                                :Art.53 ;
                        :scientificArtifactDescription "modify the attention weights after training, applying temperature scaling controlled by a hyperparameter that can be tuned to maximize some fairness metric. The hyperparameter can either increase entropy to focus on a broader set of potentially less stereotypical tokens, or can decrease entropy to attend to a narrower context, which may reduce exposure to stereotypical tokens." .


