###  http://fairness_ontology.com/UniformFairness
:UniformFairness rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                          :GroupFairnessNotion ,
                          :IndependenceFairnessNotion ,
                          :ObservationalFairnessNotion ,
                          :OutcomeFairnessNotion ,
                          :ScientificArtifact ,
                          fmo:fairness_notion ;
                 :isMeasuredBy :Variance ;
                 :isProposedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2021_WU> ;
                 :isUsedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2021_WU> ;
                 :scientificArtifactDescription """A recommendation result has  the property of uniform fair exposure for providers if each provider receives exposure ($e_p$) proportional to the number of items it offers ($I_p$), i.e., $\\frac{e_{p_1}}{\\lvert I_{p_1} \\rvert} = \\frac{e_{p_2}}{\\lvert I_{p_2} \\rvert},
\\quad \\forall\\, p_1, p_2 \\in P $, where P is the set of providers. Note that providers can be seen as groups of items. Hence, this is a group fairness notion.""" .


