###  http://fairness_ontology.com/rKL
:rKL rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
              :GranularityMetric ,
              :ItemFocusedMetric ,
              :OptimizationObjectMetric ,
              :RecommendationSystemMetric ,
              :ScientificArtifact ,
              :SingleGranularityMetric ,
              :SubjectMetric ,
              :TreatmentFocusedMetric ,
              fmo:fairness_metric ;
     :isProposedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2017_YANG> ;
     :isUsedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2017_YANG> ;
     :measures :DemographicParity ,
               :StatisticalParity .


###  http://fairness_ontology.com/rND
:rND rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
              :GranularityMetric ,
              :ItemFocusedMetric ,
              :OptimizationObjectMetric ,
              :RecommendationSystemMetric ,
              :ScientificArtifact ,
              :SingleGranularityMetric ,
              :SubjectMetric ,
              :TreatmentFocusedMetric ,
              fmo:fairness_metric ;
     :isProposedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2017_YANG> ;
     :isUsedBy <http://fairness_ontology.com/2017_YANG> ;
     :measures :DemographicParity ,
               :StatisticalParity ;
     skos:definition "(*)Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain is a ranking metric used to evaluate recommendation systems by measuring the quality of the ranked list of recommended items. It assesses a system's ability to place the most relevant items at the top of the list, with higher scores indicating a better ranking. NDCG is calculated by dividing the Discounted Cumulative Gain (DCG) of the actual recommendation list by the DCG of an ideal list, resulting in a score between 0 and 1." .


